<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's July 1-23 coconut oil exports 72,500 T.</title>
<headline>Manila's July 1-23 coconut oil exports 72,500 T.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine coconut oil exports between July 1 and 23 reached 72,500 tonnes, up 21.5 percent compared with 59,671 tonnes shipped in the whole of July last year, trade group United Coconut Association of the Philippines Inc (UCAP) said on Monday.  </p>
<p>UCAP said in a report the Philippines also exported 27,000 tonnes of copra meal between July 1 and 23.</p>
<p>It said preliminary exports of Philippine coconut products in the first seven months of the year reached 862,619 tonnes in copra terms against an actual 855,046 in the year period.</p>
<p>Besides coconut oil and copra meal, the Philippines export dehydrated coconut meat and oleochemicals.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (63 2) 841-8936, Fax 817-6267</p>
